<title>HONG KONG: Tomorrow year profit up 0.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Tomorrow year profit up 0.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended October 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   17.8   vs 22.0 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0    vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    71.90  vs 71.61</p>
<p>    Turnover		     578.26 vs 454.37</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tomorrow International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 11-17</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Tomorrow International is an electronic products maker.</p>
<p>Share earnings are based on the weighted average of 403.16 million shares vs 324.93 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is eight H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs five cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
